steps.text:
Oh, no, no. {{It was nothing}}. I was so nervous my hands were shaking.
Sure. I was taught to stay modest. If I just say “thank you,” I feel like I’m showing off.
OK… {{That’s so kind of you to say.}}
Thanks, {{I’m glad you liked it}}. But {{I can’t take all the credit}}. The developers built the prototype in two days, and you prepared all the data.
Well, {{I learned from the best}}. I’ve been watching you run meetings for years.
Wow. {{That means a lot coming from you.}}

My upstairs neighbor runs the washing machine after midnight. I haven’t slept well in weeks. I wrote a note, but I didn’t put it up. It read like a list of grievances.
OK. Hi, {{do you have a minute?}} {{There’s something I’ve been meaning to tell you.}}
{{I don’t want to make a big deal out of it, but}} your washing machine is so loud at night. It’s really annoying.
Right. {{I’ve noticed that}} the machine runs around midnight, and I’m a light sleeper. {{I hope this doesn’t come across the wrong way.}}
Could you run it a bit earlier? {{Can we figure this out together?}}
A knock. I’ll go up tomorrow afternoon and talk to them in person.

Oh, {{I’d love to, but}} it’s my dad’s birthday. My whole family’s having lunch together.
Sorry. I feel bad saying no again. I missed the team dinner last month, too.
That’s me at work these days. {{I’ve got a lot on my plate right now.}} The client wants the new screens by April.
Even to my manager? Wouldn’t that sound rude?
OK. {{Thanks for thinking of me}}, Maya. {{I wish I could}}, but I have a prior engagement. {{Can I take a rain check?}}
Got it. I’ve got family plans, so can I take a rain check? {{Keep me in mind for next time.}}

I brought some soup. Grace, {{I’m so sorry for your loss.}}
Oh, Grace. {{I can’t imagine how hard this must be}}, so far from home.
{{There are no words.}} But he knew how much you loved him.
That’s so sweet. Want to show me some photos? {{Whenever you’re ready.}}
Look at those ears! And this one, at the beach?
Don’t apologize. {{It’s okay not to be okay.}} {{Take all the time you need.}}
{{I’m here if you need anything.}} {{I’ll drop by with some food}} tomorrow. And {{be gentle with yourself}}, OK?

Ugh, Ben. {{It’s so bad it’s good.}}
Thanks. Are these rolls homemade?
{{I walked right into that one.}}
Slow. The second-stage launch keeps getting pushed back. We’re just spinning our wheels, {{no pun intended}}.
I honestly didn’t plan it! But here’s one on purpose. I’m a designer, so I don’t tell jokes. I just draw laughs.

So we play devil’s advocate? Fun. What’s the topic?
Oh no. Okay. {{I don’t actually believe this, but}} fruit doesn’t belong on pizza.
Fine. {{For the sake of argument}}, let’s say tomatoes don’t count. They’re not sweet. Pineapple is basically dessert.
Hmm. Then {{let’s assume for a moment that}} good crust should stay crispy. Pineapple is so juicy that it makes the crust soggy. {{You can’t deny that.}}
{{Now I’m starting to convince myself!}}
Wait, that’s my real argument! Wow, {{that was harder than I thought}}.
